  "review_conclusions": [
    "Migration validates the entire target chain before callbacks; source/type/schema policy belongs to the inspected caller boundary. Callback Values are consumed and errors retain step/source ownership.",
    "Text dispatch probes the reserved envelope and keeps explicit legacy fallback separate; schema/version checks precede payload migration and target decoding. Domain validation remains caller-owned.",
    "Wire truncation, body/input size ceilings, schema mismatch and future-version errors match their actual rejection paths; physical encoding version and payload schema version remain separate.",
    "Explicit canonical output budget counts the final newline and permits exact equality; I/O and spool failures remain separate failure paths. It is not a total allocation limit.",
    "The existing 25 test functions and helpers were fully inspected. Adequate preexisting docs remain unchanged in 14 files; no assertions, callback bodies or source tests were changed."
  ],
